  "narrative": "The independent validation for H12 confirms the discovery result. H12 is signed in the positive direction, so a positive estimate means that TP53-loss cells have a less negative USP7 dependency score, i.e. weaker USP7 dependency. The discovery estimate was +0.802 with a 95% Welch interval of approximately +0.782 to +0.822, and the independent validation estimate is +0.797 with a multiplicity-aware independent interval of approximately +0.769 to +0.824. The magnitude is far above the 10% clinical-significance threshold using the overall USP7 mean scale, and the independent interval remains entirely positive and large. Therefore I accept the overall H12 association: in this dataset, TP53 loss is strongly associated with weaker USP7 dependency. I close investigation of the original overall comparison because the claim is now supported by both discovery and independent validation, although related subtype/interaction refinements can remain separate. The broader interim conclusion is: (1) supported associations include SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency, KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency with validation; (2) negative overall findings include BRAF mutation -> stronger BRAF dependency, ERBB2 amplification -> stronger ERBB2 dependency, ARID1A loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MYC amplification -> stronger POLR2A dependency, RB1 loss -> stronger KIF18A dependency, and the originally registered KEAP1 loss -> stronger NFE2L2 dependency, which was reversed; (3) unresolved overall findings include KRAS mutation vs KRAS dependency, EGFR amplification vs EGFR dependency, and TP53 loss vs MDM2 dependency, plus several deferred MYC/oncogene cross-talk hypotheses; (4) no causal claim is warranted, and external generalizability remains uncertain. The most informative next analyses are to test the registered adenocarcinoma subgroup refinements for KRAS, EGFR, MDM2, WRN, and USP7; to run the SMARCA4-by-ARID1A interaction and KEAP1-by-batch audits; and then to prioritize independent validation of the strongest unvalidated accepted claims, especially KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency because the effect is large and directionally surprising, followed by SMARCA4 -> SMARCA2 and MSI-high -> WRN.",
  "research_notes": "Interim evidence state after validation: Accepted and validated overall: H12 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency, supported by discovery R10 and validation R13; closed original overall comparison, with subtype H25 available separately. Accepted unvalidated overall: H7 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H13 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H18 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (reversed from H5). Negative/closed overall: H2 BRAF, H4 ERBB2, H5 original KEAP1 direction, H8 ARID1A -> SMARCA2, H9 MYC -> POLR2A, H14 RB1 -> KIF18A. Unresolved: H1 KRAS overall, H3 EGFR overall, H6 MDM2 TP53 loss overall, plus deferred H10 MYC -> RPL11, H11 MYC -> DHX9, H15 KRAS -> STAT3, H16 EGFR amp -> RIT1, H17 ERBB2 amp -> TMED10. Next plan: run registered refinements H19 KRAS dependency in adenocarcinoma, H20 EGFR dependency in adenocarcinoma, H21 MDM2 TP53-loss effect in adenocarcinoma, H22 SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2 dependency interaction with ARID1A loss, H23 KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency batch_a interaction, H24 WRN MSI effect in adenocarcinoma, and H25 USP7 TP53-loss effect in adenocarcinoma. Next validation priority: H18 because it is a large reversed discovery and may be technical or context-dependent; then H7 and H13 if resources permit. Keep interpretations as dataset associations and mechanism-generating, not causal or externally generalizable."
